#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Isang libreng kurso ng IBM sa quantum information at computation"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing the number of iterations"
msgstr "Pagpili ng bilang ng iterations"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore leftarrow */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore leftarrow */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have established that the state vector of the register $\\mathsf{Q}$ in Grover's algorithm remains in the two-dimensional subspace spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ once the initialization step has been performed.\n"
msgstr "Napatunayan na natin na ang state vector ng register $\\mathsf{Q}$ sa Grover's algorithm ay nananatili sa two-dimensional subspace na sinasaklaw ng $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ kapag natapos na ang initialization step.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The goal is to find an element $x\\in A_1$, and this goal will be accomplished if we can obtain the state $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — for if we measure this state, we're guaranteed to get a measurement outcome $x\\in A_1$.\n"
"Given that the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ after $t$ iterations in step 2 is\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang layunin ay mahanap ang isang elemento $x\\in A_1$, at maaabot ito kung makukuha natin ang state $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — dahil kapag sinukat natin ang state na ito, garantisadong makukuha natin ang measurement outcome na $x\\in A_1$.\n"
"Dahil ang state ng $\\mathsf{Q}$ pagkatapos ng $t$ iterations sa step 2 ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "we should choose $t$ so that\n"
msgstr "dapat nating piliin ang $t$ upang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle A_1 \\vert G^t \\vert u \\rangle =\n"
"\\sin((2t + 1)\\theta)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle A_1 \\vert G^t \\vert u \\rangle =\n"
"\\sin((2t + 1)\\theta)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is as close to $1$ as possible in absolute value, to maximize the probability to obtain $x\\in A_1$ from the measurement.\n"
"For any angle $\\theta \\in (0,2\\pi)$, the value $\\sin((2t + 1)\\theta)$ *oscillates* as $t$ increases, though it is not necessarily periodic — there's no guarantee that we'll ever get the same value twice.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay maging kalapit ng $1$ hangga't maaari sa absolute value, para mapalaki ang probabilidad na makakuha ng $x\\in A_1$ mula sa measurement.\n"
"Para sa anumang anggulo $\\theta \\in (0,2\\pi)$, ang halaga ng $\\sin((2t + 1)\\theta)$ ay *nag-o-oscillate* habang tumataas ang $t$, kahit hindi ito kailangang peryodiko — walang garantiya na makukuha natin ang parehong halaga ng dalawang beses.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Naturally, in addition to making the probability of obtaining an element $x\\in A_1$ from the measurement large, we would also like to choose $t$ to be as small as possible, because $t$ applications of the operation $G$ requires $t$ queries to the function $f$.\n"
"Because we're aiming to make $\\sin( (2t + 1) \\theta)$ close to $1$ in absolute value, a natural way to do this is to choose $t$ so that\n"
msgstr ""
"Natural na, bukod sa pagiging malaki ng probabilidad na makakuha ng elemento $x\\in A_1$ mula sa measurement, nais din nating piliin ang pinakamaliit na $t$ hangga't maaari, dahil ang $t$ na aplikasyon ng operasyon $G$ ay nangangailangan ng $t$ na queries sa function $f$.\n"
"Dahil layunin nating gawing malapit sa $1$ ang $\\sin( (2t + 1) \\theta)$ sa absolute value, isang natural na paraan ay ang pumili ng $t$ upang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(2t + 1) \\theta \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(2t + 1) \\theta \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving for $t$ yields\n"
msgstr "Kapag sinolve para sa $t$ makukuha natin ang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} - \\frac{1}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} - \\frac{1}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, $t$ must be an integer, so we won't necessarily be able to hit this value exactly — but what we can do is to take the closest integer to this value, which is\n"
msgstr "Siyempre, dapat integer ang $t$, kaya hindi natin palaging maaabot nang eksakto ang halagang ito — ngunit ang magagawa natin ay ang kumuha ng pinakamalapit na integer sa halagang ito, na kung saan ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\Bigr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\Bigr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the recommended number of iterations for Grover's algorithm.\n"
"As we proceed with the analysis, we'll see that the closeness of this integer to the target value naturally affects the performance of the algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ang inirerekomendang bilang ng iterations para sa Grover's algorithm.\n"
"Habang tinatapusin ang pagsusuri, makikita natin na ang pagiging malapit ng integer na ito sa target na halaga ay natural na nakakaapekto sa performance ng algorithm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(As an aside, if the target value $\\pi/(4\\theta) - 1/2$ happens to be exactly half-way between two integers, this expression of $t$ is what we get by rounding up. We could alternatively round down, which makes sense to do because it means one fewer query — but this is secondary and unimportant for the sake of the lesson.)\n"
msgstr "(Bilang paalala, kung ang target na halaga na $\\pi/(4\\theta) - 1/2$ ay eksaktong nasa kalagitnaan ng dalawang integer, ang expression na ito ng $t$ ang makukuha sa pamamagitan ng pag-round up. Maaari ring i-round down, na mas makatuwirang gawin dahil nangangahulugang isang query na mas kaunti — ngunit ito ay pangalawa at hindi mahalaga para sa layunin ng aralin.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recalling that the value of the angle $\\theta$ is given by the formula\n"
msgstr "Alalahanin na ang halaga ng anggulo $\\theta$ ay ibinibigay ng formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"we see that the recommended number of iterations $t$ depends on the number of strings in $A_1$.\n"
"This presents a challenge if we don't know how many solutions we have, as we'll discuss later.\n"
msgstr ""
"makikita natin na ang inirerekomendang bilang ng iterations na $t$ ay nakasalalay sa bilang ng mga string sa $A_1$.\n"
"Nagdudulot ito ng hamon kung hindi natin alam kung gaano karaming solusyon mayroon tayo, tulad ng tatalakayin natin sa ibang pagkakataon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unique search {#unique-search}"
msgstr "Natatanging paghahanap {#unique-search}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's focus on the situation in which there's a single string $x$ such that $f(x)=1$.\n"
"Another way to say this is that we're considering an instance of the *Unique search* problem.\n"
"In this case we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, tukuyin natin ang sitwasyon kung saan mayroon lamang isang string na $x$ na $f(x)=1$.\n"
"Isa pang paraan ng pagsabi nito ay isinasaalang-alang natin ang isang instance ng problema ng *Unique search*.\n"
"Sa kasong ito mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which can be conveniently approximated as\n"
msgstr "na maaaring maginhawang i-approximate bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}} \\biggr) \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}} \\biggr) \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"when $N$ gets large.\n"
"If we substitute $\\theta = 1/\\sqrt{N}$ into the expression\n"
msgstr ""
"kapag nagiging malaki ang $N.$\n"
"Kung papalitan natin ng $\\theta = 1/\\sqrt{N}$ sa expression na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\Bigr\\rfloor\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\Bigr\\rfloor\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "we obtain\n"
msgstr "makukuha natin\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\sqrt{N} \\Bigr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\sqrt{N} \\Bigr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recalling that $t$ is not only the number of times the operation $G$ is performed, but also the number of queries to the function $f$ required by the algorithm, we see that we're on track to obtaining an algorithm that requires $O(\\sqrt{N})$ queries.\n"
msgstr "Alalahanin na ang $t$ ay hindi lamang ang bilang ng beses na ginagawa ang operasyon $G$, kundi pati na rin ang bilang ng queries sa function $f$ na kailangan ng algorithm, kaya nakikita nating papalapit na tayo sa pagkuha ng algorithm na nangangailangan ng $O(\\sqrt{N})$ na queries.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll investigate how well the recommended choice of $t$ works.\n"
"The probability that the final measurement results in the unique solution can be expressed explicitly as\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay susuriin natin kung gaano kahusay ang inirerekomendang pagpili ng $t.$\n"
"Ang probabilidad na ang panghuling measurement ay magreresulta sa natatanging solusyon ay maaaring ipahayag nang malinaw bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,1) = \\sin^2 \\bigl( (2t + 1) \\theta \\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,1) = \\sin^2 \\bigl( (2t + 1) \\theta \\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first argument, $N$, refers to the number of items we're searching over, and the second argument, which is $1$ in this case, refers to the number of solutions.\n"
"A bit later we'll use the same notation more generally, where there are multiple solutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang argument, $N,$ ay tumutukoy sa bilang ng mga item na hinahanap natin, at ang pangalawang argument, na $1$ sa kasong ito, ay tumutukoy sa bilang ng mga solusyon.\n"
"Kalaunan ay gagamitin natin ang parehong notasyon nang mas pangkalahataan, kung saan may maramihang solusyon.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here's a table of the probabilities of success for increasing values of $N = 2^n$.\n"
msgstr "Narito ang isang talahanayan ng mga probabilidad ng tagumpay para sa mga tumataas na halaga ng $N = 2^n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & p(N,1)\\\\ \\hline\n"
"2\t& 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"4\t& 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t& 0.9453125000\\\\\n"
"16\t& 0.9613189697\\\\\n"
"32\t& 0.9991823155\\\\\n"
"64\t& 0.9965856808\\\\\n"
"128\t& 0.9956198657\\\\\n"
"256\t& 0.9999470421\\\\\n"
"512\t& 0.9994480262\\\\\n"
"1024 &\t 0.9994612447\\\\\n"
"2048 &\t 0.9999968478\\\\\n"
"4096 &\t 0.9999453461\\\\\n"
"8192 &\t 0.9999157752\\\\\n"
"16384 &\t 0.9999997811\\\\\n"
"32768 &\t 0.9999868295\\\\\n"
"65536 &\t 0.9999882596\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & p(N,1)\\\\ \\hline\n"
"2\t& 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"4\t& 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t& 0.9453125000\\\\\n"
"16\t& 0.9613189697\\\\\n"
"32\t& 0.9991823155\\\\\n"
"64\t& 0.9965856808\\\\\n"
"128\t& 0.9956198657\\\\\n"
"256\t& 0.9999470421\\\\\n"
"512\t& 0.9994480262\\\\\n"
"1024 &\t 0.9994612447\\\\\n"
"2048 &\t 0.9999968478\\\\\n"
"4096 &\t 0.9999453461\\\\\n"
"8192 &\t 0.9999157752\\\\\n"
"16384 &\t 0.9999997811\\\\\n"
"32768 &\t 0.9999868295\\\\\n"
"65536 &\t 0.9999882596\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that these probabilities are not strictly increasing.\n"
"In particular, we have an interesting anomaly when $N=4$, where we get a solution with certainty.\n"
"It can, however, be proved in general that\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin na ang mga probabilidad na ito ay hindi mahigpit na tumataas.\n"
"Partikular na, may kagiliw-giliw na anomalya kapag $N=4$, kung saan nakakakuha tayo ng solusyon nang may katiyakan.\n"
"Ngunit maaaring mapatunayan sa pangkalahatan na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,1) \\geq 1 - \\frac{1}{N}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,1) \\geq 1 - \\frac{1}{N}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for all $N$, so the probability of success goes to $1$ in the limit as $N$ becomes large, as the values above seem to suggest.\n"
"This is good!\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa lahat ng $N$, kaya ang probabilidad ng tagumpay ay papalapit sa $1$ sa limitasyon habang nagiging malaki ang $N$, tulad ng iminumungkahi ng mga halagang nabanggit sa itaas.\n"
"Maganda ito!\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"But notice, however, that even a weak bound such as $p(N,1) \\geq 1/2$ establishes the utility of Grover's algorithm.\n"
"For whatever measurement outcome $x$ we obtain from running the procedure, we can always check to see if $f(x) = 1$ using a single query to $f$.\n"
"And if we fail to obtain the unique string $x$ for which $f(x) = 1$ with probability at most $1/2$ by running the procedure once, then after $m$ independent runs of the procedure we will have failed to obtain this unique string $x$ with probability at most $2^{-m}$.\n"
"That is, using $O(m \\sqrt{N})$ queries to $f$, we'll obtain the unique solution $x$ with probability at least $1 - 2^{-m}$.\n"
"Using the better bound $p(N,1) \\geq 1 - 1/N$ reveals that the probability to find $x\\in A_1$ using this method is actually at least $1 - N^{-m}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngunit pansinin, gayunpaman, na kahit isang mahinang hangganan tulad ng $p(N,1) \\geq 1/2$ ay nagpapatunay ng utility ng Grover's algorithm.\n"
"Para sa anumang measurement outcome na $x$ na makukuha natin mula sa pagpapatakbo ng pamamaraan, palagi nating masusuri kung $f(x) = 1$ gamit ang isang query sa $f$.\n"
"At kung mabigo tayong makuha ang natatanging string $x$ na $f(x) = 1$ na may probabilidad na hindi hihigit sa $1/2$ sa isang pagpapatakbo ng pamamaraan, pagkatapos ng $m$ na magkakalayong pagpapatakbo ng pamamaraan ay mabibigo tayong makuha ang natatanging string $x$ na ito na may probabilidad na hindi hihigit sa $2^{-m}$.\n"
"Ibig sabihin, gamit ang $O(m \\sqrt{N})$ na queries sa $f$, makukuha natin ang natatanging solusyon $x$ na may probabilidad na hindi bababa sa $1 - 2^{-m}$.\n"
"Gamit ang mas mahusay na hangganan na $p(N,1) \\geq 1 - 1/N$ makikita na ang probabilidad ng paghanap ng $x\\in A_1$ gamit ang pamamaraang ito ay talagang hindi bababa sa $1 - N^{-m}$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple solutions {#multiple-solutions}"
msgstr "Maramihang solusyon {#multiple-solutions}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the number of elements in $A_1$ varies, so too does the angle $\\theta$, which can have a significant effect on the algorithm's probability of success.\n"
"For the sake of brevity, let's write $s = \\vert A_1 \\vert$ to denote the number of solutions, and as before we'll assume that $s\\geq 1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang nagbabago ang bilang ng mga elemento sa $A_1$, nagbabago rin ang anggulo $\\theta$, na maaaring magkaroon ng malaking epekto sa probabilidad ng tagumpay ng algorithm.\n"
"Para sa brevity, isulat natin ang $s = \\vert A_1 \\vert$ upang tukuyin ang bilang ng mga solusyon, at tulad ng dati ay ipagpalagay nating $s\\geq 1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a motivating example, let's imagine that we have $s = 4$ solutions rather than a single solution, as we considered above.\n"
"This means that\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang motivating example, isipin natin na mayroon tayong $s = 4$ na solusyon sa halip na isang solusyon, tulad ng tiningnan natin sa itaas.\n"
"Ibig sabihin nito\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is approximately double the angle we had in the $\\vert A_1 \\vert = 1$ case when $N$ is large.\n"
"Suppose that we didn't know any better, and selected the same value of $t$ as in the unique solution setting:\n"
msgstr ""
"na halos doble ng anggulo na mayroon tayo sa kaso ng $\\vert A_1 \\vert = 1$ kapag malaki ang $N.$\n"
"Ipagpalagay nating hindi natin alam nang mas mabuti, at pinili ang parehong halaga ng $t$ tulad sa setting ng natatanging solusyon:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Biggl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\sin^{-1}\\bigl(1/\\sqrt{N}\\bigr)}\\Biggr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Biggl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\sin^{-1}\\bigl(1/\\sqrt{N}\\bigr)}\\Biggr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The effect will be catastrophic as the following table of probabilities reveals.\n"
msgstr "Ang epekto ay magiging mapaminsala tulad ng ipinapakita ng sumusunod na talahanayan ng mga probabilidad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & \\text{Success probability}\\\\ \\hline\n"
"4\t& 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t& 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"16\t& 0.2500000000\\\\\n"
"32\t& 0.0122070313\\\\\n"
"64\t& 0.0203807689\\\\\n"
"128\t& 0.0144530758\\\\\n"
"256\t& 0.0000705058\\\\\n"
"512\t& 0.0019310741\\\\\n"
"1024\t& 0.0023009083\\\\\n"
"2048\t& 0.0000077506\\\\\n"
"4096\t& 0.0002301502\\\\\n"
"8192\t& 0.0003439882\\\\\n"
"16384\t& 0.0000007053\\\\\n"
"32768\t& 0.0000533810\\\\\n"
"65536\t& 0.0000472907\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & \\text{Success probability}\\\\ \\hline\n"
"4\t& 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t& 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"16\t& 0.2500000000\\\\\n"
"32\t& 0.0122070313\\\\\n"
"64\t& 0.0203807689\\\\\n"
"128\t& 0.0144530758\\\\\n"
"256\t& 0.0000705058\\\\\n"
"512\t& 0.0019310741\\\\\n"
"1024\t& 0.0023009083\\\\\n"
"2048\t& 0.0000077506\\\\\n"
"4096\t& 0.0002301502\\\\\n"
"8192\t& 0.0003439882\\\\\n"
"16384\t& 0.0000007053\\\\\n"
"32768\t& 0.0000533810\\\\\n"
"65536\t& 0.0000472907\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This time the probability of success goes to $0$ as $N$ goes to infinity.\n"
"This happens because we're effectively rotating twice as fast as we did when there was a unique solution, so we end up zooming past the target $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ and landing near $-\\vert A_0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pagkakataong ito ang probabilidad ng tagumpay ay papalapit sa $0$ habang lumalaki ang $N$.\n"
"Nangyayari ito dahil epektibo tayong umiikot nang doble ang bilis kumpara sa noong may natatanging solusyon, kaya nalalampasan natin ang target na $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ at napupunta malapit sa $-\\vert A_0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, if instead we use the recommended choice of $t$, which is\n"
msgstr "Gayunpaman, kung gagamitin natin ang inirerekomendang pagpili ng $t$, na kung saan ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta}\\Bigr\\rfloor\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta}\\Bigr\\rfloor\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "para sa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"then the performance will be better.\n"
"To be more precise, using this choice of $t$ leads to success with high probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"mas maganda ang magiging performance.\n"
"Upang maging mas tiyak, ang paggamit ng pagpiling ito ng $t$ ay nagdudulot ng tagumpay na may mataas na probabilidad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & p(N,4)\\\\ \\hline\n"
"4\t & 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t & 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"16\t & 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"32\t & 0.9453125000\\\\\n"
"64\t & 0.9613189697\\\\\n"
"128\t & 0.9991823155\\\\\n"
"256\t & 0.9965856808\\\\\n"
"512\t & 0.9956198657\\\\\n"
"1024\t& 0.9999470421\\\\\n"
"2048\t& 0.9994480262\\\\\n"
"4096\t& 0.9994612447\\\\\n"
"8192\t& 0.9999968478\\\\\n"
"16384\t& 0.9999453461\\\\\n"
"32768\t& 0.9999157752\\\\\n"
"65536\t& 0.9999997811\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & p(N,4)\\\\ \\hline\n"
"4\t & 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t & 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"16\t & 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"32\t & 0.9453125000\\\\\n"
"64\t & 0.9613189697\\\\\n"
"128\t & 0.9991823155\\\\\n"
"256\t & 0.9965856808\\\\\n"
"512\t & 0.9956198657\\\\\n"
"1024\t& 0.9999470421\\\\\n"
"2048\t& 0.9994480262\\\\\n"
"4096\t& 0.9994612447\\\\\n"
"8192\t& 0.9999968478\\\\\n"
"16384\t& 0.9999453461\\\\\n"
"32768\t& 0.9999157752\\\\\n"
"65536\t& 0.9999997811\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generalizing what was claimed earlier, it can be proved that\n"
msgstr "Ginagawang pangkalahataan ang nabanggit nang mas maaga, maaaring mapatunayan na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,s) \\geq 1 - \\frac{s}{N},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,s) \\geq 1 - \\frac{s}{N},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where we're using the notation suggested earlier: $p(N,s)$ denotes the probability that Grover's algorithm run for $t$ iterations reveals a solution when there are $s$ solutions in total out of $N$ possibilities.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ginagamit natin ang notasyong iminungkahi nang mas maaga: ang $p(N,s)$ ay tumutukoy sa probabilidad na ang Grover's algorithm na pinatakbo para sa $t$ na iterations ay magsisiwalat ng solusyon kapag mayroon $s$ na solusyon sa kabuuan mula sa $N$ na posibilidad.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This lower bound of $1 - s/N$ on the probability of success is slightly peculiar in that more solutions implies a worse lower bound — but under the assumption that $s$ is significantly smaller than $N$, we nevertheless conclude that the probability of success is reasonably high.\n"
"As before, the mere fact that $p(N,s)$ is reasonably large implies the algorithm's usefulness.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang lower bound na ito na $1 - s/N$ sa probabilidad ng tagumpay ay medyo kakaiba dahil ang mas maraming solusyon ay nagbibigay ng mas masamang lower bound — ngunit sa ilalim ng pagpapalagay na ang $s$ ay makabuluhang mas maliit kaysa $N$, maaari pa ring masabi natin na ang probabilidad ng tagumpay ay medyo mataas.\n"
"Tulad ng dati, ang katotohanan lamang na ang $p(N,s)$ ay medyo malaki ay nagpapatunay ng utility ng algorithm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It also happens to be the case that\n"
msgstr "Nangyayari rin na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,s) \\geq \\frac{s}{N}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,s) \\geq \\frac{s}{N}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This lower bound describes the probability that a string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ selected uniformly at random is a solution — so Grover's algorithm always does at least as well as random guessing.\n"
"(In fact, when $t=0$, Grover's algorithm *is* random guessing.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang lower bound na ito ay naglalarawan ng probabilidad na ang isang string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ na pinili nang random ay isang solusyon — kaya ang Grover's algorithm ay palaging hindi bababa sa random guessing.\n"
"(Sa katunayan, kapag $t=0$, ang Grover's algorithm *ay* random guessing.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's take a look at the number of iterations (and hence the number of queries)\n"
msgstr "Ngayon tingnan natin ang bilang ng iterations (at samakatuwid ang bilang ng queries)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta}\\Bigr\\rfloor,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta}\\Bigr\\rfloor,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For every $\\alpha \\in [0,1]$, it is the case that $\\sin^{-1}(\\alpha)\\geq \\alpha$,\n"
"and so\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa bawat $\\alpha \\in [0,1]$, totoo na ang $\\sin^{-1}(\\alpha)\\geq \\alpha$,\n"
"kaya\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}\\right) \\geq \\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}\\right) \\geq \\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This implies that\n"
msgstr "Ipinapahiwatig nito na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\sqrt{\\frac{N}{s}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\sqrt{\\frac{N}{s}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This translates to a savings in the number of queries as $s$ grows.\n"
"In particular, the number of queries required is\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagdudulot ito ng pagtitipid sa bilang ng queries habang lumalaki ang $s.$\n"
"Partikular na, ang kinakailangang bilang ng queries ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{N}{s}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{N}{s}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unknown number of solutions {#unknown-number-of-solutions}"
msgstr "Hindi kilalang bilang ng solusyon {#unknown-number-of-solutions}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the number of solutions $s = \\vert A_1 \\vert$ is *unknown*, then a different approach is required, for in this situation we have no knowledge of $s$ to inform our choice of $t$.\n"
"There are, in fact, multiple approaches.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang bilang ng mga solusyon na $s = \\vert A_1 \\vert$ ay *hindi kilala*, kailangan ng ibang diskarte, dahil sa sitwasyong ito wala tayong kaalaman sa $s$ na magbibigay-impormasyon sa ating pagpili ng $t$.\n"
"Sa katunayan, mayroon pang maraming diskarte.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One simple approach is to choose\n"
msgstr "Isang simpleng diskarte ay ang pumili ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t \\in \\Bigl\\{ 1,\\ldots,\\bigl\\lfloor\\pi\\sqrt{N}/4\\bigr\\rfloor \\Bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t \\in \\Bigl\\{ 1,\\ldots,\\bigl\\lfloor\\pi\\sqrt{N}/4\\bigr\\rfloor \\Bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*uniformly at random*.\n"
"Selecting $t$ in this way always finds a solution (assuming one exists) with probability greater than 40%, though this is not obvious and requires an analysis that will not be included here.\n"
"It does makes sense, however, particularly when we think about the geometric picture:\n"
"rotating the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ a random number of times like this is not unlike choosing a random unit vector in the space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$, for which it is likely that the coefficient of $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ is reasonably large.\n"
"By repeating this procedure and checking the outcome in the same way as described before, the probability to find a solution can be made very close to $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"nang *random na pantay-pantay*.\n"
"Ang pagpili ng $t$ sa ganitong paraan ay palaging nakakahanap ng solusyon (kung mayroon man) na may probabilidad na higit sa 40%, kahit hindi ito halata at nangangailangan ng pagsusuri na hindi isasama dito.\n"
"Makatuwiran naman ito, partikular na kapag iniisip natin ang geometric na larawan:\n"
"ang pag-ikot ng state ng $\\mathsf{Q}$ nang random na bilang ng beses tulad nito ay hindi iba sa pagpili ng random na unit vector sa space na sinasaklaw ng $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle$, na para sa mga iyon ay malamang na malaki ang coefficient ng $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
"Sa pamamagitan ng pag-uulit ng pamamaraang ito at pagsusuri ng outcome sa parehong paraan tulad ng inilarawan nang mas maaga, ang probabilidad na mahanap ang solusyon ay maaaring gawing malapit sa $1$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a refined method that finds a solution when one exists using $O(\\sqrt{N/s})$ queries, even when the number of solutions $s$ is not known, and requires $O(\\sqrt{N})$ queries to determine that there are no solutions when $s=0$.\n"
msgstr "Mayroong isang pinahusay na pamamaraan na nakakahanap ng solusyon kapag mayroon gamit ang $O(\\sqrt{N/s})$ na queries, kahit hindi kilala ang bilang ng solusyon na $s$, at nangangailangan ng $O(\\sqrt{N})$ na queries upang matukoy na walang solusyon kapag $s=0$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic idea is to choose $t$ uniformly at random from the set $\\{1,\\ldots,T\\}$ iteratively, for increasing values of $T$.\n"
"In particular, we can start with $T = 1$ and increase it exponentially, always terminating the process as soon as a solution is found and capping $T$ so as not to waste queries when there isn't a solution.\n"
"The process takes advantage of the fact that fewer queries are required when more solutions exist.\n"
"Some care is required, however, to balance the rate of growth of $T$ with the probability of success for each iteration.\n"
"(Taking $T \\leftarrow \\lceil \\frac{5}{4}T\\rceil$ works, for instance, as an analysis reveals.\n"
"Doubling $T$, however, does not — this turns out to be too fast of an increase.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangunahing ideya ay ang pumili ng $t$ nang random mula sa set na $\\{1,\\ldots,T\\}$ nang paulit-ulit, para sa mga tumataas na halaga ng $T$.\n"
"Partikular na, maaari tayong magsimula sa $T = 1$ at taasan ito nang exponential, palaging tinatatapos ang proseso sa sandaling mahanap ang solusyon at nililimitahan ang $T$ upang hindi masayang ang mga queries kapag walang solusyon.\n"
"Ginagamit ng proseso ang katotohanan na mas kaunting queries ang kailangan kapag mas maraming solusyon.\n"
"Ngunit kailangan ng ilang pag-iingat upang balansehin ang rate ng paglaki ng $T$ sa probabilidad ng tagumpay para sa bawat iteration.\n"
"(Ang paggamit ng $T \\leftarrow \\lceil \\frac{5}{4}T\\rceil$ ay gumagana, halimbawa, tulad ng ipinapakita ng pagsusuri.\n"
"Ang pag-double ng $T$, gayunpaman, ay hindi gumagana — ito pala ay masyadong mabilis na pagtaas.)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The trivial cases {#the-trivial-cases}"
msgstr "Ang mga trivial na kaso {#the-trivial-cases}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Throughout the analysis we've just gone through, we've assumed that the number of solutions is non-zero.\n"
"Indeed, by referring to the vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa buong pagsusuri na ginawa natin ngayon, ipinagpalagay natin na ang bilang ng mga solusyon ay hindi zero.\n"
"Sa katunayan, sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy sa mga vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"we have implicitly assumed that $A_0$ and $A_1$ are both nonempty.\n"
"Here we will briefly consider what happens when one of these sets is empty.\n"
msgstr ""
"impliside nating ipinagpalagay na ang $A_0$ at $A_1$ ay parehong hindi walang laman.\n"
"Dito natin titingnan nang maikli kung ano ang nangyayari kapag isa sa mga set na ito ay walang laman.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we bother with an analysis, let's observe the obvious:\n"
"if every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ is a solution, then we'll see a solution when we measure; and when there aren't any solutions, we won't see one.\n"
"In some sense there's no need to go deeper than this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago pa man natin simulan ang pagsusuri, pansinin ang halata:\n"
"kung bawat string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ ay isang solusyon, makikita natin ang solusyon kapag nasukat natin; at kapag walang solusyon, hindi natin makikita ang isa.\n"
"Sa ilang paraan ay hindi na kailangang pumunta pa nang mas malalim kaysa dito.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can, however, quickly verify the mathematics for these trivial cases.\n"
"The situation where one of $A_0$ and $A_1$ is empty happens when $f$ is constant;\n"
"$A_1$ is empty when $f(x) = 0$ for every $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, and $A_0$ is empty when $f(x) = 1$ for every $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
"This means that\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating, gayunpaman, mabilis na i-verify ang matematika para sa mga trivial na kasong ito.\n"
"Ang sitwasyon kung saan isa sa $A_0$ at $A_1$ ay walang laman ay nangyayari kapag constant ang $f$;\n"
"ang $A_1$ ay walang laman kapag $f(x) = 0$ para sa bawat $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ at ang $A_0$ ay walang laman kapag $f(x) = 1$ para sa bawat $x\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
"Ibig sabihin nito\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_f \\vert u\\rangle = \\pm \\vert u\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_f \\vert u\\rangle = \\pm \\vert u\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and therefore\n"
msgstr "at samakatuwid\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f\\vert u\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\pm \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert u\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\pm \\vert u\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f\\vert u\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\pm \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert u\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\pm \\vert u\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So, irrespective of the number of iterations $t$ we perform in these cases, the measurements will always reveal a uniform random string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
msgstr "Kaya, anuman ang bilang ng iterations na $t$ na ginagawa natin sa mga kasong ito, ang mga measurement ay palaging magsisiwalat ng uniform random string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
